the Central Mosque in Simferopol the  Crimean Tatars meet here for Friday  prayers the Muslim minority here feels  especially threatened by Russian  sabre-rattling you can imagine what the  mood is like here kids are asking their  parents whether there will be a war  everyone is frightened the Crimean  Tatars pray hoping against hope that  history won't repeat itself in 1944 the  Soviet leader Joseph Stalin ordered that  the Tatars be deported on mass from the  peninsula  they were resettled in Siberia and  Central Asia many still harbor fierce  hatred for Russia following prayers the  Tatar leader in Crimea's parliament  referred chubarov addressed his people  he made an urgent call for unity and  calm asking for a boycott of a planned  referendum on independence of the region  even though chubarov is a member of the  regional parliament he considers the  body's actions to be illegal the risk of  the situation escalating is high he says  more wood wood was nurtured in the could  lead to bloodshed for all ethnic groups  in the Crimean region we call on the UN  to take action and send peacekeepers to  the region as quickly as possible  middle school boys it's exceptional and  it shows the tension and the fear that  the political leader of the tatar  minority here in the region is talking  to its people right inside the mosque  after the prayers his main message is  that the international community has to  get much more involved here in the  region to prevent the situation from  getting even worse
 

